y&rsquo;s 6 grids in Mercer County came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years for November to December, the most of any pair of months since 1951. In 2025, August to September on the middle of the grids came in at 42% of normal. So far in 2026, the middle ran 40% of normal in February to March and 151% in April to May. Every grid&rsquo;s driest year was 1988, with grid 24745 at 46% of normal.</p>"}
